The loop invariant itself advanced, but the entry claim could not reuse it because I had over-specialized the module scope to empty; after loading, that scope necessarily contains the `common` closure. I’m generalizing that preserved scope to an arbitrary unchanged map. This is a framing correction, not an execution abstraction.
